NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000646 "1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000647 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000648 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000650 "=encoding UTF-8"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000651 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000652 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000653 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000654 "Test::Deep - Extremely flexible deep comparison"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000655 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000656 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000657 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000658 "version 1.205"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000659 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000660 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000661 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000662 "  use Test::More tests => $Num_Tests;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000663 "  use Test::Deep;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000664 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000665 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000666 "    $actual_horrible_nested_data_structure,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000667 "    $expected_horrible_nested_data_structure,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000668 "    \"got the right horrible nested data structure\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000669 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000670 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000671 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000672 "    $object,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000673 "    methods(name => \"John\", phone => \"55378008\"),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000674 "    \"object methods ok\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000675 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000676 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000677 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000678 "    \\@array,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000679 "    [$hash1, $hash2, ignore()],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000680 "    \"first 2 elements are as expected, ignoring 3\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000681 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000682 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000683 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000684 "    $object,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000685 "    noclass({value => 5}),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000686 "    \"object looks ok, not checking its class\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000687 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000688 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000689 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000690 "    \\@result,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000691 "    bag('a', 'b', {key => [1, 2]}),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000692 "    \"array has the 3 things we wanted in some order\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000693 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000694 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000695 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000696 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000697 "If you don't know anything about automated testing in Perl then you should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000698 "probably read about L<Test::Simple> and L<Test::More> before preceding."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000699 "Test::Deep uses the L<Test::Builder> framework."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000700 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000701 "Test::Deep gives you very flexible ways to check that the result you got is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000702 "the result you were expecting. At its simplest it compares two structures"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000703 "by going through each level, ensuring that the values match, that arrays and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000704 "hashes have the same elements and that references are blessed into the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000705 "correct class. It also handles circular data structures without getting"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000706 "caught in an infinite loop."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000707 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000708 "Where it becomes more interesting is in allowing you to do something besides"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000709 "simple exact comparisons. With strings, the C<eq> operator checks that 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000710 "strings are exactly equal but sometimes that's not what you want. When you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000711 "don't know exactly what the string should be but you do know some things"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000712 "about how it should look, C<eq> is no good and you must use pattern matching"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000713 "instead. Test::Deep provides pattern matching for complex data structures"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000714 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000715 "Test::Deep has B<I<a lot>> of exports.  See L</EXPORTS> below."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000716 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000717 "=head1 PERL VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000718 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000719 "This library should run on perls released even a long time ago.  It should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000720 "work on any version of perl released in the last five years."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000721 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000722 "Although it may work on older versions of perl, no guarantee is made that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000723 "minimum required version will not be increased.  The version may be increased"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000724 "for any reason, and there is no promise that patches will be accepted to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000725 "lower the minimum required perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000726 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000727 "=head1 EXAMPLES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000728 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000729 "How Test::Deep works is much easier to understand by seeing some examples."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000730 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000731 "=head2 Without Test::Deep"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000732 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000733 "Say you want to test a function which returns a string. You know that your"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000734 "string should be a 7 digit number beginning with 0, C<eq> is no good in this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000735 "situation, you need a regular expression. So you could use Test::More's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000736 "C<like()> function:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000737 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000738 "  like($string, qr/^0[0-9]{6}$/, \"number looks good\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000739 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000740 "Similarly, to check that a string looks like a name, you could do:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000741 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000742 "  like($string, qr/^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$/,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000743 "    \"got title, first and last name\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000744 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000745 "Now imagine your function produces a hash with some personal details in it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000746 "You want to make sure that there are 2 keys, Name and Phone and that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000747 "name looks like a name and the phone number looks like a phone number. You"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000748 "could do:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000749 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000750 "  $hash = make_person();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000751 "  like($hash->{Name}, qr/^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$/, \"name ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000752 "  like($hash->{Phone}, qr/^0[0-9]{6}$/, \"phone ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000753 "  is(scalar keys %$hash, 2, \"correct number of keys\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000754 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000755 "But that's not quite right, what if make_person has a serious problem and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000756 "didn't even return a hash? We really need to write"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000757 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000758 "  if (ref($hash) eq \"HASH\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000759 "  {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000760 "    like($hash->{Name}, qr/^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$/, \"name ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000761 "    like($hash->{Phone}, qr/^0[0-9]{6}$/, \"phone ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000762 "    is(scalar keys %$hash, 2, \"correct number of keys\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000763 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000764 "  else"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000765 "  {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000766 "    fail(\"person not a hash\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000767 "    fail(\"person not a hash\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000768 "    fail(\"person not a hash\"); # need 3 to keep the plan correct"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000769 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000770 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000771 "Already this is getting messy, now imagine another entry in the hash, an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000772 "array of children's names. This would require"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000773 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000774 "  if (ref($hash) eq \"HASH\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000775 "  {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000776 "    like($hash->{Name}, $name_pat, \"name ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000777 "    like($hash->{Phone}, '/^0d{6}$/', \"phone ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000778 "    my $cn = $hash->{ChildNames};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000779 "    if (ref($cn) eq \"ARRAY\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000780 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000781 "      foreach my $child (@$cn)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000782 "      {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000783 "        like($child, $name_pat);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000784 "      }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000785 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000786 "    else"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000787 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000788 "        fail(\"child names not an array\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000789 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000790 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000791 "  else"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000792 "  {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000793 "    fail(\"person not a hash\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000794 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000795 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000796 "This is a horrible mess and because we don't know in advance how many"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000797 "children's names there will be, we can't make a plan for our test anymore"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000798 "(actually, we could but it would make things even more complicated)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000799 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000800 "Test::Deep to the rescue."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000801 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000802 "=head2 With Test::Deep"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000803 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000804 "  my $name_re = re('^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000805 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000806 "    $person,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000807 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000808 "      Name => $name_re,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000809 "      Phone => re('^0d{6}$'),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000810 "      ChildNames => array_each($name_re)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000811 "    },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000812 "    \"person ok\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000813 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000814 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000815 "This will do everything that the messy code above does and it will give a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000816 "sensible message telling you exactly what went wrong if it finds a part of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000817 "$person that doesn't match the pattern. C<re()> and C<array_each()> are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000818 "special function imported from Test::Deep. They create a marker that tells"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000819 "Test::Deep that something different is happening here. Instead of just doing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000820 "a simple comparison and checking are two things exactly equal, it should do"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000821 "something else."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000822 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000823 "If a person was asked to check that 2 structures are equal, they could print"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000824 "them both out and compare them line by line. The markers above are similar"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000825 "to writing a note in red pen on one of the printouts telling the person that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000826 "for this piece of the structure, they should stop doing simple line by line"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000827 "comparison and do something else."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000828 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000829 "C<re($regex)> means that Test::Deep should check that the current piece of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000830 "data matches the regex in C<$regex>. C<array_each($struct)> means that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000831 "Test::Deep should expect the current piece of data to be an array and it"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000832 "should check that every element of that array matches C<$struct>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000833 "In this case, every element of C<< $person->{ChildNames} >> should look like a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000834 "name. If say the 3rd one didn't you would get an error message something"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000835 "like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000836 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000837 "  Using Regexp on $data->{ChildNames}[3]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000838 "     got    : 'Queen John Paul Sartre'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000839 "     expect : /^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$/"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000840 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000841 "There are lots of other special comparisons available, see"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000842 "L<SPECIAL COMPARISONS PROVIDED> below for the full list."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000843 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000844 "=head2 Reusing structures"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000845 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000846 "Test::Deep is good for reusing test structures so you can do this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000847 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000848 "  my $name_re = re('^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000849 "  my $person_cmp = {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000850 "    Name => $name_re,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000851 "    Phone => re('^0d{6}$'),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000852 "    ChildNames => array_each($name_re)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000853 "  };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000854 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000855 "  cmp_deeply($person1, $person_cmp, \"person ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000856 "  cmp_deeply($person2, $person_cmp, \"person ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000857 "  cmp_deeply($person3, $person_cmp, \"person ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000858 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000859 "You can even put $person_cmp in a module and let other people use it when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000860 "they are writing test scripts for modules that use your modules."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000861 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000862 "To make things a little more difficult, lets change the person data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000863 "structure so that instead of a list of ChildNames, it contains a list of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000864 "hashes, one for each child. So in fact our person structure will contain"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000865 "other person structures which may contain other person structures and so on."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000866 "This is easy to handle with Test::Deep because Test::Deep structures can"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000867 "include themselves. Simply do"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000868 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000869 "  my $name_re = re('^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000870 "  my $person_cmp = {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000871 "    Name => $name_re,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000872 "    Phone => re('^0d{6}$'),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000873 "    # note no mention of Children here"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000874 "  };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000875 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000876 "  $person_cmp->{Children} = array_each($person_cmp);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000877 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000878 "  cmp_deeply($person, $person_cmp, \"person ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000879 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000880 "This will now check that $person->{Children} is an array and that every"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000881 "element of that array also matches C<$person_cmp>, this includes checking"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000882 "that its children also match the same pattern and so on."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000883 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000884 "=head2 Circular data structures"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000885 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000886 "A circular data structure is one which loops back on itself, you can make"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000887 "one easily by doing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000888 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000889 "  my @b;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000890 "  my @a = (1, 2, 3, \\@b);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000891 "  push(@b, \\@a);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000892 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000893 "now C<@a> contains a reference to be C<@b> and C<@b> contains a reference to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000894 "C<@a>. This causes problems if you have a program that wants to look inside"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000895 "C<@a> and keep looking deeper and deeper at every level, it could get caught"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000896 "in an infinite loop looking into C<@a> then C<@b> then C<@a> then C<@b> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000897 "so on."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000898 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000899 "Test::Deep avoids this problem so we can extend our example further by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000900 "saying that a person should also list their parents."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000901 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000902 "  my $name_re = re('^(Mr|Mrs|Miss) \\w+ \\w+$');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000903 "  my $person_cmp = {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000904 "    Name => $name_re,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000905 "    Phone => re('^0d{6}$'),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000906 "    # note no mention of Children here"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000907 "  };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000908 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000909 "  $person_cmp->{Children} = each_array($person_cmp);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000910 "  $person_cmp->{Parents} = each_array($person_cmp);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000911 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000912 "  cmp_deeply($person, $person_cmp, \"person ok\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000913 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000914 "So this will check that for each child C<$child> in C<< $person->{Children} >>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000915 "that the C<< $child->{Parents} >> matches C<$person_cmp> however it is smart"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000916 "enough not to get caught in an infinite loop where it keeps bouncing between"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000917 "the same Parent and Child."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000918 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000919 "=head1 TERMINOLOGY"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000920 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000921 "C<cmp_deeply($got, $expected, $name)> takes 3 arguments. C<$got> is the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000922 "structure that you are checking, you must not include any special"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000923 "comparisons in this structure or you will get a fatal error. C<$expected>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000924 "describes what Test::Deep will be looking for in $got. You can put special"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000925 "comparisons in $expected if you want to."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000926 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000927 "As Test::Deep descends through the 2 structures, it compares them one piece"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000928 "at a time, so at any point in the process, Test::Deep is thinking about 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000929 "things - the current value from C<$got> and the current value from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000930 "C<$expected>. In the documentation, I call them C<$got_v> and C<exp_v>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000931 "respectively."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000932 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000933 "=head1 COMPARISON FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000934 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000935 "=head3 cmp_deeply"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000936 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000937 "  my $ok = cmp_deeply($got, $expected, $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000938 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000939 "C<$got> is the result to be checked. C<$expected> is the structure against"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000940 "which C<$got> will be check. C<$name> is the test name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000941 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000942 "This is the main comparison function, the others are just wrappers around"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000943 "this.  C<$got> and C<$expected> are compared recursively.  Each value in"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000944 "C<$expected> defines what's expected at the corresponding location in C<$got>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000945 "Simple scalars are compared with C<eq>.  References to structures like hashes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000946 "and arrays are compared recursively."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000947 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000948 "Items in C<$expected>, though, can also represent complex tests that check for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000949 "numbers in a given range, hashes with at least a certain set of keys, a string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000950 "matching a regex, or many other things."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000951 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000952 "See L</WHAT ARE SPECIAL COMPARISONS> for details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000953 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000954 "=head3 cmp_bag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000955 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000956 "  my $ok = cmp_bag(\\@got, \\@bag, $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000957 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000958 "Is shorthand for cmp_deeply(\\@got, bag(@bag), $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000959 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000960 "I<n.b.>: Both arguments must be array refs. If they aren't an exception will be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000961 "thrown."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000962 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000963 "=head3 cmp_set"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000964 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000965 "  my $ok = cmp_set(\\@got, \\@set, $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000966 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000967 "Is shorthand for cmp_deeply(\\@got, set(@set), $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000968 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000969 "=head3 cmp_methods"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000970 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000971 "  my $ok = cmp_methods(\\@got, \\@methods, $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000972 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000973 "Is shorthand for cmp_deeply(\\@got, methods(@methods), $name)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000974 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000975 "=head3 eq_deeply"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000976 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000977 "  my $ok = eq_deeply($got, $expected)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000978 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000979 "This is the same as cmp_deeply() except it just returns true or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000980 "false. It does not create diagnostics or talk to L<Test::Builder>, but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000981 "if you want to use it in a non-testing environment then you should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000982 "import it through L<Test::Deep::NoTest>. For example"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000983 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000984 "  use Test::Deep::NoTest;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000985 "  print \"a equals b\" unless eq_deeply($a, $b);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000986 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000987 "otherwise the L<Test::Builder> framework will be loaded and testing messages"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000988 "will be output when your program ends."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000989 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000990 "=head3 cmp_details"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000991 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000992 "  ($ok, $stack) = cmp_details($got, $expected)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000993 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000994 "This behaves much like eq_deeply, but it additionally allows you to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000995 "produce diagnostics in case of failure by passing the value in C<$stack>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000996 "to C<deep_diag>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000997 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000998 "Do not make assumptions about the structure or content of C<$stack> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000999 "do not use it if C<$ok> contains a true value."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001000 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001001 "See L</USING TEST::DEEP WITH TEST::BUILDER> for example uses."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001002 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001003 "=head1 SPECIAL COMPARISONS PROVIDED"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001004 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001005 "In the documentation below, C<$got_v> is used to indicate any given value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001006 "within the C<$got> structure."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001007 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001008 "=head3 ignore"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001009 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001010 "  cmp_deeply( $got, ignore() );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001011 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001012 "This makes Test::Deep skip tests on C<$got_v>. No matter what value C<$got_v>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001013 "has, Test::Deep will think it's correct. This is useful if some part of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001014 "structure you are testing is very complicated and already tested elsewhere,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001015 "or if it is unpredictable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001016 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001017 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001018 "    $got,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001019 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001020 "      name    => 'John',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001021 "      random  => ignore(),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001022 "      address => [ '5 A street', 'a town', 'a country' ],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001023 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001024 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001025 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001026 "is the equivalent of checking"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001027 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001028 "  $got->{name} eq 'John';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001029 "  exists $got->{random};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001030 "  cmp_deeply($got->{address}, ['5 A street', 'a town', 'a country']);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001031 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001032 "=head3 methods"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001033 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001034 "  cmp_deeply( $got, methods(%hash) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001036 "%hash is a hash of method call => expected value pairs."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001037 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001038 "This lets you call methods on an object and check the result of each call."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001039 "The methods will be called in the order supplied. If you want to pass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001040 "arguments to the method you should wrap the method name and arguments in an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001041 "array reference."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001042 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001043 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001044 "    $obj,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001045 "    methods(name => \"John\", [\"favourite\", \"food\"] => \"taco\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001046 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001047 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001048 "is roughly the equivalent of checking that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001049 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001050 "  $obj->name eq \"John\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001051 "  $obj->favourite(\"food\") eq \"taco\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001052 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001053 "The methods will be called in the order you supply them and will be called"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001054 "in scalar context. If you need to test methods called in list context then"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001055 "you should use C<listmethods()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001056 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001057 "B<NOTE> Just as in a normal test script, you need to be careful if the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001058 "methods you call have side effects like changing the object or other objects"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001059 "in the structure. Although the order of the methods is fixed, the order of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001060 "some other tests is not so if C<$expected> is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001061 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001062 "  {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001063 "    manager => methods(@manager_methods),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001064 "    coder => methods(@coder_methods)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001065 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001066 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001067 "there is no way to know which if manager and coder will be tested first. If"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001068 "the methods you are testing depend on and alter global variables or if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001069 "manager and coder are the same object then you may run into problems."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001070 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001071 "=head3 listmethods"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001072 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001073 "  cmp_deeply( $got, listmethods(%hash) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001074 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001075 "C<%hash> is a hash of pairs mapping method names to expected return values."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001076 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001077 "This is almost identical to methods() except the methods are called in list"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001078 "context instead of scalar context. This means that the expected return"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001079 "values supplied must be in array references."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001080 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001081 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001082 "    $obj,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001083 "    listmethods("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001084 "      name => [ \"John\" ],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001085 "      [\"favourites\", \"food\"] => [\"Mapo tofu\", \"Gongbao chicken\"]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001086 "    )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001087 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001088 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001089 "is the equivalent of checking that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001090 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001091 "  cmp_deeply([$obj->name], [\"John\"]);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001092 "  cmp_deeply([$obj->favourites(\"food\")], [\"Mapo tofu\", \"Gongbao chicken\"]);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001093 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001094 "The methods will be called in the order you supply them."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001095 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001096 "B<NOTE> The same caveats apply as for methods()."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001097 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001098 "=head3 shallow"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001100 "  cmp_deeply( $got, shallow($thing) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001101 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001102 "C<$thing> is a ref."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001103 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001104 "This prevents Test::Deep from looking inside C<$thing>. It allows you to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001105 "check that C<$got_v> and C<$thing> are references to the same variable. So"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001106 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001107 "  my @a = @b = (1, 2, 3);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001108 "  cmp_deeply(\\@a, \\@b);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001109 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001110 "will pass because C<@a> and C<@b> have the same elements however"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001111 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001112 "  cmp_deeply(\\@a, shallow(\\@b))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001113 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001114 "will fail because although C<\\@a> and C<\\@b> both contain C<1, 2, 3> they are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001115 "references to different arrays."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001116 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001117 "=head3 noclass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001118 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001119 "  cmp_deeply( $got, noclass($thing) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001120 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001121 "C<$thing> is a structure to be compared against."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001122 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001123 "This makes Test::Deep ignore the class of objects, so it just looks at the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001124 "data they contain. Class checking will be turned off until Test::Deep is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001125 "finished comparing C<$got_v> against C<$thing>. Once Test::Deep comes out of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001126 "C<$thing> it will go back to its previous setting for checking class."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001127 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001128 "This can be useful when you want to check that objects have been"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001129 "constructed correctly but you don't want to write lots of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001130 "C<bless>es. If C<@people> is an array of Person objects then"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001131 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001132 "  cmp_deeply(\\@people, ["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001133 "    bless {name => 'John', phone => '555-5555'}, \"Person\","
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001134 "    bless {name => 'Anne', phone => '444-4444'}, \"Person\","
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001135 "  ]);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001136 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001137 "can be replaced with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001138 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001139 "  cmp_deeply(\\@people, noclass(["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001140 "    {name => 'John', phone => '555-5555'},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001141 "    {name => 'Anne', phone => '444-4444'}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001142 "  ]));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001143 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001144 "However, this is testing so you should also check that the objects are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001145 "blessed correctly. You could use a map to bless all those hashes or you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001146 "could do a second test like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001147 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001148 "  cmp_deeply(\\@people, array_each(isa(\"Person\"));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001149 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001150 "=head3 useclass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001151 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001152 "  cmp_deeply( $got, useclass($thing) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001153 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001154 "This turns back on the class comparison while inside a C<noclass()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001155 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001156 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001157 "    $got,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001158 "    noclass("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001159 "      ["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001160 "        useclass( $object )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001161 "      ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001162 "    )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001163 "  )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001164 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001165 "In this example the class of the array reference in C<$got> is ignored but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001166 "the class of C<$object> is checked, as is the class of everything inside"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001167 "C<$object>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001169 "=head3 re"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001170 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001171 "  cmp_deeply( $got, re($regexp, $capture_data, $flags) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001172 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001173 "C<$regexp> is either a regular expression reference produced with C<qr/.../>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001174 "or a string which will be used to construct a regular expression."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001175 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001176 "C<$capture_data> is optional and is used to check the strings captured by an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001177 "regex. This should can be an array ref or a Test::Deep comparator that works"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001178 "on array refs."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001179 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001180 "C<$flags> is an optional string which controls whether the regex runs as a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001181 "global match. If C<$flags> is \"g\" then the regex will run as C<m/$regexp/g>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001182 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001183 "Without C<$capture_data>, this simply compares C<$got_v> with the regular"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001184 "expression provided. So"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001185 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001186 "  cmp_deeply($got, [ re(\"ferg\") ])"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001187 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001188 "is the equivalent of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001189 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001190 "  $got->[0] =~ /ferg/"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001191 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001192 "With C<$capture_data>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001193 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001194 "  cmp_deeply($got, [re($regex, $capture_data)])"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001195 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001196 "is the equivalent of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001197 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001198 "  my @data = $got->[0] =~ /$regex/;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001199 "  cmp_deeply(\\@data, $capture_data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001200 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001201 "So you can do something simple like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001202 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001203 "  cmp_deeply($got, re(qr/(\\d\\d)(\\w\\w)/, [25, \"ab\" ]))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001204 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001205 "to check that C<(\\d\\d)> was 25 and C<(\\w\\w)> was \"ab\" but you can also use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001206 "Test::Deep objects to do more complex testing of the captured values"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001207 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001208 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001209 "    \"cat=2,dog=67,sheep=3,goat=2,dog=5\","
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001210 "    re("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001211 "      qr/(\\D+)=\\d+,?/,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001212 "      set(qw( cat sheep dog )),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001213 "      \"g\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001214 "    ),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001215 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001216 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001217 "here, the regex will match the string and will capture the animal names and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001218 "check that they match the specified set, in this case it will fail,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001219 "complaining that \"goat\" is not in the set."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001220 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001221 "=head3 all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001222 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001223 "  cmp_deeply( $got, all(@expecteds) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001224 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001225 "C<@expecteds> is an array of expected structures."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001226 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001227 "This allows you to compare data against multiple expected results and make"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001228 "sure each of them matches."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001229 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001230 "  cmp_deeply($got, all(isa(\"Person\"), methods(name => 'John')))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001231 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001232 "is equivalent to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001233 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001234 "  $got->isa(\"Person\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001235 "  $got->name eq 'John'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001236 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001237 "If either test fails then the whole thing is considered a fail. This is a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001238 "short-circuit test, the testing is stopped after the first failure, although"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001239 "in the future it may complete all tests so that diagnostics can be output"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001240 "for all failures. When reporting failure, the parts are counted from 1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001241 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001242 "Thanks to the magic of overloading, you can write"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001243 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001244 "  any( re(\"^wi\"), all(isa(\"Person\"), methods(name => 'John')) )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001245 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001246 "as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001247 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001248 "   re(\"^wi\") | isa(\"Person\") & methods(name => 'John')"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001249 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001250 "Note B<single> C<|> not double, as C<||> cannot be overloaded. This will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001251 "only work when there is a special comparison involved. If you write"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001252 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001253 "  \"john\" | \"anne\" | \"robert\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001254 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001255 "Perl will turn this into"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001256 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001257 "  \"{onort\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001258 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001259 "which is presumably not what you wanted. This is because perl ors them"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001260 "together as strings before Test::Deep gets a chance to do any overload"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001261 "tricks."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001262 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001263 "=head3 any"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001264 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001265 "  cmp_deeply( $got, any(@expecteds) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001266 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001267 "C<@expecteds> is an array of expected structures."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001268 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001269 "This can be used to compare data against multiple expected results and make"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001270 "sure that at least one of them matches. This is a short-circuit test so if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001271 "a test passes then none of the tests after that will be attempted."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001272 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001273 "You can also use overloading with C<|> similarly to all()."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001274 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001275 "=head3 Isa"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001276 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001277 "  cmp_deeply( $got, Isa($class) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001278 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001279 "=head3 isa"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001280 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001281 "  cmp_deeply( $got, isa($class) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001282 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001283 "C<$class> is a class name."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001284 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001285 "This uses C<UNIVERSAL::isa()> to check that C<$got_v> is blessed into the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001286 "class C<$class>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001287 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001288 "B<NOTE:> C<Isa()> does exactly as documented here, but C<isa()> is slightly"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001289 "different. If C<isa()> is called with 1 argument it falls through to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001290 "C<Isa()>. If C<isa()> called with 2 arguments, it falls through to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001291 "C<UNIVERSAL::isa>. This is to prevent breakage when you import C<isa()> into"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001292 "a package that is used as a class. Without this, anyone calling"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001293 "C<Class-E<gt>isa($other_class)> would get the wrong answer. This is a hack"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001294 "to patch over the fact that C<isa> is exported by default."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001295 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001296 "=head3 obj_isa"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001297 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001298 "  cmp_deeply( $got, obj_isa($class) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001299 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001300 "This test accepts only objects that are instances of C<$class> or a subclass."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001301 "Unlike the C<Isa> test, this test will never accept class names."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001302 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001303 "=head3 array_each"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001304 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001305 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, array_each($thing) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001306 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001307 "C<$thing> is a structure to be compared against."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001308 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001309 "<$got_v> must be an array reference. Each element of it will be compared to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001310 "C<$thing>. This is useful when you have an array of similar things, for example"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001311 "objects of a known type and you don't want to have to repeat the same test"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001312 "for each one."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001313 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001314 "  my $common_tests = all("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001315 "     isa(\"MyFile\"),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001316 "     methods("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001317 "       handle => isa(\"IO::Handle\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001318 "       filename => re(\"^/home/ted/tmp\"),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001319 "    )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001320 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001321 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001322 "  cmp_deeply($got, array_each($common_tests));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001323 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001324 "is similar to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001325 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001326 "  foreach my $got_v (@$got) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001327 "    cmp_deeply($got_v, $common_tests)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001328 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001329 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001330 "Except it will not explode if C<$got> is not an array reference. It will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001331 "check that each of the objects in C<@$got> is a MyFile and that each one"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001332 "gives the correct results for its methods."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001333 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001334 "You could go further, if for example there were 3 files and you knew the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001335 "size of each one you could do this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001336 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001337 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001338 "    $got,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001339 "    all("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001340 "      array_each($common_tests),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001341 "      ["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001342 "        methods(size => 1000),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001343 "        methods(size => 200),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001344 "        methods(size => 20)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001345 "      ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001346 "    )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001347 "  )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001348 "  cmp_deeply($got, array_each($structure));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001349 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001350 "=head3 hash_each"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001351 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001352 "  cmp_deeply( \\%got, hash_each($thing) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001353 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001354 "This test behaves like C<array_each> (see above) but tests that each hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001355 "value passes its tests."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001356 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001357 "=head3 str"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001359 "  cmp_deeply( $got, str($string) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001360 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001361 "$string is a string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001362 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001363 "This will stringify C<$got_v> and compare it to C<$string> using C<eq>, even"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001364 "if C<$got_v> is a ref. It is useful for checking the stringified value of an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001365 "overloaded reference."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001366 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001367 "=head3 num"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001368 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001369 "  cmp_deeply( $got, num($number, $tolerance) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001370 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001371 "C<$number> is a number."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001372 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001373 "C<$tolerance> is an optional number."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001374 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001375 "This will add 0 to C<$got_v> and check if it's numerically equal to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001376 "C<$number>, even if C<$got_v> is a ref. It is useful for checking the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001377 "numerical value of an overloaded reference. If C<$tolerance> is supplied"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001378 "then this will check that C<$got_v> and C<$exp_v> are less than"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001379 "C<$tolerance> apart. This is useful when comparing floating point numbers as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001380 "rounding errors can make it hard or impossible for C<$got_v> to be exactly"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001381 "equal to C<$exp_v>. When C<$tolerance> is supplied, the test passes if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001382 "C<abs($got_v - $exp_v) <= $tolerance>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001383 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001384 "B<Note> in Perl, C<\"12blah\" == 12> because Perl will be smart and convert"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001385 "\"12blah\" into 12. You may not want this. There was a strict mode but that is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001386 "now gone. A \"looks like a number\" test will replace it soon. Until then you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001387 "can usually just use the string() comparison to be more strict. This will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001388 "work fine for almost all situations, however it will not work when <$got_v>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001389 "is an overloaded value who's string and numerical values differ."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001390 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001391 "=head3 bool, true, false"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001392 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001393 "  cmp_deeply( $got, bool($value) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001394 "  cmp_deeply( $got, true );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001395 "  cmp_deeply( $got, false );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001396 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001397 "C<$value> is anything you like but it's probably best to use 0 or 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001398 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001399 "This will check that C<$got_v> and C<$value> have the same truth value, that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001400 "is they will give the same result when used in boolean context, like in an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001401 "C<if()> statement."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001402 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001403 "B<Note:> C<true> and C<false> are only imported by special request."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001404 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001405 "=head3 code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001406 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001407 "  cmp_deeply( $got, code(\\&subref) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001408 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001409 "C<\\&subref> is a reference to a subroutine which will be passed a single"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001410 "argument, it then should return a true or false and possibly a string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001411 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001412 "This will pass C<$got_v> to the subroutine which returns true or false to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001413 "indicate a pass or fail. Fails can be accompanied by a diagnostic string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001414 "which gives an explanation of why it's a fail."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001416 "  sub check_name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001417 "  {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001418 "    my $name = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001419 "    if ($boss->likes($name))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001420 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001421 "      return 1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001422 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001423 "    else"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001424 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001425 "      return (0, \"the boss doesn't like your name\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001426 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001427 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001428 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001429 "  cmp_deeply(\"Brian\", code(\\&check_name));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001430 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001431 "=head2 SET COMPARISONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001432 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001433 "Set comparisons give special semantics to array comparisons:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001434 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001435 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001436 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001437 "=item * The order of items in a set is irrelevant"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001438 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001439 "=item * The presence of duplicate items in a set is ignored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001440 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001441 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001442 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001443 "As such, in any set comparison, the following arrays are equal:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001444 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001445 "  [ 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001446 "  [ 1, 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001447 "  [ 1, 2, 1 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001448 "  [ 2, 1, 1 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001449 "  [ 1, 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001450 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001451 "All are interpreted by C<set> semantics as if the set was only specified as:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001452 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001453 "  [ 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001454 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001455 "All C<set> functions return an object which can have additional items added to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001456 "it:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001457 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001458 "  my $set = set( 1, 2 );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001459 "  $set->add(1, 3, 1 );  # Set is now ( 1, 2, 3 )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001460 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001461 "Special care must be taken when using special comparisons within sets. See"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001462 "L</SPECIAL CARE WITH SPECIAL COMPARISONS IN SETS AND BAGS> for details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001463 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001464 "=head3 set"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001465 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001466 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, set(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001467 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001468 "This does a set comparison, that is, it compares two arrays but ignores the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001469 "order of the elements and it ignores duplicate elements, but ensures that all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001470 "items in C<@elements> will be in C<$got> and all items in C<$got> will be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001471 "in C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001472 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001473 "So the following tests will be passes, and will be equivalent:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001474 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001475 "  cmp_deeply([1, 2, 2, 3], set(3, 2, 1, 1));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001476 "  cmp_deeply([1, 2, 3],    set(3, 2, 1));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001477 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001478 "=head3 supersetof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001479 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001480 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, supersetof(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001481 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001482 "This function works much like L<< C<set>|/set >>, and performs a set comparison"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001483 "of C<$got_v> with the elements of C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001484 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001485 "C<supersetof> is however slightly relaxed, such that C<$got> may contain things"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001486 "not in C<@elements>, but must at least contain all C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001487 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001488 "These two statements are equivalent, and will be passes:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001489 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001490 "  cmp_deeply([1,2,3,3,4,5], supersetof(2,2,3));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001491 "  cmp_deeply([1,2,3,4,5],   supersetof(2,3));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001492 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001493 "But these will be failures:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001494 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001495 "  cmp_deeply([1,2,3,4,5],   supersetof(2,3,6)); # 6 not in superset"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001496 "  cmp_deeply([1],           supersetof(1,2));   # 2 not in superset"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001497 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001498 "=head3 subsetof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001499 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001500 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, subsetof(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001501 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001502 "This function works much like L<< C<set>|/set >>, and performs a set comparison"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001503 "of C<$got_v> with the elements of C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001504 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001505 "This is the inverse of C<supersetof>, which expects all unique elements found"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001506 "in C<$got_v> must be in C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001507 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001508 "  cmp_deeply([1,2,4,5], subsetof(2,3,3)    ) # Fail: 1,4 & 5 extra"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001509 "  cmp_deeply([2,3,3],   subsetof(1,2,4,5)  ) # Fail: 3 extra"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001510 "  cmp_deeply([2,3,3],   subsetof(1,2,4,5,3)) # Pass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001511 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001512 "=head3 none"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001513 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001514 "  cmp_deeply( $got, none(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001515 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001516 "@elements is an array of elements, wherein no elements in C<@elements> may"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001517 "be equal to C<$got_v>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001518 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001519 "=head3 noneof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001520 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001521 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, noneof(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001522 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001523 "@elements is an array of elements, wherein no elements in C<@elements> may be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001524 "found in C<$got_v>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001525 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001526 "For example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001528 "  # Got has no 1, no 2, and no 3"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001529 "  cmp_deeply( [1], noneof( 1, 2, 3 ) ); # fail"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001530 "  cmp_deeply( [5], noneof( 1, 2, 3 ) ); # pass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001532 "=head2 BAG COMPARISONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001534 "Bag comparisons give special semantics to array comparisons, that are similar"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001535 "to L<< set comparisons|/SET COMPARISONS >>, but slightly different."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001536 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001537 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001538 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001539 "=item * The order of items in a bag is irrelevant"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001540 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001541 "=item * The presence of duplicate items in a bag is B<PRESERVED>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001542 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001543 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001544 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001545 "As such, in any bag comparison, the following arrays are equal:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001546 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001547 "  [ 1, 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001548 "  [ 1, 2, 1 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001549 "  [ 2, 1, 1 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001550 "  [ 1, 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001551 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001552 "However, they are B<NOT> equal to any of the following:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001553 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001554 "  [ 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001555 "  [ 1, 2, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001556 "  [ 1, 1, 1, 2 ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001557 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001558 "All C<bag> functions return an object which can have additional items added to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001559 "it:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001560 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001561 "  my $bag = bag( 1, 2 );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001562 "  $bag->add(1, 3, 1 );  # Bag is now ( 1, 1, 1, 2, 3 )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001563 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001564 "Special care must be taken when using special comparisons within bags. See"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001565 "L</SPECIAL CARE WITH SPECIAL COMPARISONS IN SETS AND BAGS> for details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001566 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001567 "=head3 bag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001568 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001569 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, bag(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001570 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001571 "This does an order-insensitive bag comparison between C<$got> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001572 "C<@elements>, ensuring that:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001573 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001574 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001575 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001576 "=item each item in C<@elements> is found in C<$got>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001577 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001578 "=item the number of times a C<$expected_v> is found in C<@elements> is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001579 "reflected in C<$got>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001580 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001581 "=item no items are found in C<$got> other than those in C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001582 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001583 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001584 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001585 "As such, the following are passes, and are equivalent to each other:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001586 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001587 "  cmp_deeply([1, 2, 2], bag(2, 2, 1))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001588 "  cmp_deeply([2, 1, 2], bag(2, 2, 1))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001589 "  cmp_deeply([2, 2, 1], bag(2, 2, 1))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001590 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001591 "But the following are failures:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001592 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001593 "  cmp_deeply([1, 2, 2],     bag(2, 2, 1, 1)) # Not enough 1's in Got"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001594 "  cmp_deeply([1, 2, 2, 1],  bag(2, 2, 1)   ) # Too many   1's in Got"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001595 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001596 "=head3 superbagof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001597 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001598 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, superbagof( @elements ) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001599 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001600 "This function works much like L<< C<bag>|/bag >>, and performs a bag comparison"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001601 "of C<$got_v> with the elements of C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001602 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001603 "C<superbagof> is however slightly relaxed, such that C<$got> may contain things"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001604 "not in C<@elements>, but must at least contain all C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001605 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001606 "So:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001607 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001608 "  # pass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001609 "  cmp_deeply( [1, 1, 2], superbagof( 1 )      );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001610 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001611 "  # fail: not enough 1's in superbag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001612 "  cmp_deeply( [1, 1, 2], superbagof( 1, 1, 1 ));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001613 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001614 "=head3 subbagof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001615 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001616 "  cmp_deeply( \\@got, subbagof(@elements) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001617 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001618 "This function works much like L<< C<bag>|/bag >>, and performs a bag comparison"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001619 "of C<$got_v> with the elements of C<@elements>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001620 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001621 "This is the inverse of C<superbagof>, and expects all elements in C<$got> to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001622 "be in C<@elements>, while allowing items to exist in C<@elements> that are not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001623 "in C<$got>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001624 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001625 "  # pass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001626 "  cmp_deeply( [1],        subbagof( 1, 1, 2 ) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001627 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001628 "  # fail: too many 1's in subbag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001629 "  cmp_deeply( [1, 1, 1],  subbagof( 1, 1, 2 ) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001630 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001631 "=head2 HASH COMPARISONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001632 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001633 "Typically, if you're doing simple hash comparisons,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001634 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001635 "  cmp_deeply( \\%got, \\%expected )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001636 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001637 "is sufficient. C<cmp_deeply> will ensure C<%got> and C<%hash> have identical"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001638 "keys, and each key from either has the same corresponding value."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001639 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001640 "=head3 superhashof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001641 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001642 "  cmp_deeply( \\%got, superhashof(\\%hash) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001643 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001644 "This will check that the hash C<%$got> is a \"super-hash\" of C<%hash>. That"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001645 "is that all the key and value pairs in C<%hash> appear in C<%$got> but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001646 "C<%$got> can have extra ones also."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001647 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001648 "For example"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001650 "  cmp_deeply({a => 1, b => 2}, superhashof({a => 1}))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001651 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001652 "will pass but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001653 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001654 "  cmp_deeply({a => 1, b => 2}, superhashof({a => 1, c => 3}))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001655 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001656 "will fail."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001657 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001658 "=head3 subhashof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001659 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001660 "  cmp_deeply( \\%got, subhashof(\\%hash) );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001661 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001662 "This will check that the hash C<%$got> is a \"sub-hash\" of C<%hash>. That is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001663 "that all the key and value pairs in C<%$got> also appear in C<%hash>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001664 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001665 "For example"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001666 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001667 "  cmp_deeply({a => 1}, subhashof({a => 1, b => 2}))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001668 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001669 "will pass but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001670 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001671 "  cmp_deeply({a => 1, c => 3}, subhashof({a => 1, b => 2}))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001672 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001673 "will fail."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001674 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001675 "=head1 DIAGNOSTIC FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001676 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001677 "=head3 deep_diag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001678 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001679 "  my $reason = deep_diag($stack);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001680 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001681 "C<$stack> is a value returned by cmp_details.  Do not call this function"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001682 "if cmp_details returned a true value for C<$ok>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001683 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001684 "C<deep_diag()> returns a human readable string describing how the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001685 "comparison failed."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001686 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001687 "=head1 ANOTHER EXAMPLE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001688 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001689 "You've written a module to handle people and their film interests. Say you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001690 "have a function that returns an array of people from a query, each person is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001691 "a hash with 2 keys: Name and Age and the array is sorted by Name. You can do"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001692 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001693 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001694 "    $result,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001695 "    ["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001696 "      {Name => 'Anne', Age => 26},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001697 "      {Name => \"Bill\", Age => 47}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001698 "      {Name => 'John', Age => 25},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001699 "    ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001700 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001701 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001702 "Soon after, your query function changes and all the results now have an ID"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001703 "field. Now your test is failing again because you left out ID from each of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001704 "the hashes. The problem is that the IDs are generated by the database and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001705 "you have no way of knowing what each person's ID is. With Test::Deep you can"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001706 "change your query to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001707 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001708 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001709 "    $result,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001710 "    ["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001711 "      {Name => 'John', Age => 25, ID => ignore()},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001712 "      {Name => 'Anne', Age => 26, ID => ignore()},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001713 "      {Name => \"Bill\", Age => 47, ID => ignore()}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001714 "    ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001715 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001716 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001717 "But your test still fails. Now, because you're using a database, you no"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001718 "longer know what order the people will appear in. You could add a sort into"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001719 "the database query but that could slow down your application. Instead you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001720 "can get Test::Deep to ignore the order of the array by doing a bag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001721 "comparison instead."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001722 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001723 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001724 "    $result,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001725 "    bag("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001726 "      {Name => 'John', Age => 25, ID => ignore()},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001727 "      {Name => 'Anne', Age => 26, ID => ignore()},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001728 "      {Name => \"Bill\", Age => 47, ID => ignore()}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001729 "    )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001730 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001731 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001732 "Finally person gets even more complicated and includes a new field called"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001733 "Movies, this is a list of movies that the person has seen recently, again"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001734 "these movies could also come back in any order so we need a bag inside our"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001735 "other bag comparison, giving us something like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001736 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001737 "  cmp_deeply("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001738 "  $result,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001739 "    bag("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001740 "      {Name => 'John', Age => 25, ID => ignore(), Movies => bag(...)},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001741 "      {Name => 'Anne', Age => 26, ID => ignore(), Movies => bag(...)},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001742 "      {Name => \"Bill\", Age => 47, ID => ignore(), Movies => bag(...)}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001743 "    )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001744 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001745 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001746 "=head1 USING TEST::DEEP WITH TEST::BUILDER"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001747 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001748 "Combining C<cmp_details> and C<deep_diag> makes it possible to use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001749 "Test::Deep in your own test classes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001750 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001751 "In a L<Test::Builder> subclass, create a test method in the following"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001752 "form:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001753 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001754 "  sub behaves_ok {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001755 "    my $self = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001756 "    my $expected = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001757 "    my $test_name = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001758 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001759 "    my $got = do_the_important_work_here();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001760 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001761 "    my ($ok, $stack) = cmp_details($got, $expected);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001762 "    unless ($Test->ok($ok, $test_name)) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001763 "      my $diag = deep_diag($stack);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001764 "      $Test->diag($diag);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001765 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001766 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001767 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001768 "As the subclass defines a test class, not tests themselves, make sure it"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001769 "uses L<Test::Deep::NoTest>, not C<Test::Deep> itself."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001770 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001771 "=head1 LIMITATIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001772 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001773 "Currently any CODE, GLOB or IO refs will be compared using shallow(), which"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001774 "means only their memory addresses are compared."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001775 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001776 "=head1 BUGS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001777 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001778 "There is a bug in set and bag compare to do with competing SCs. It only"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001779 "occurs when you put certain special comparisons inside bag or set"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001780 "comparisons you don't need to worry about it. The full details are in the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001781 "C<bag()> docs. It will be fixed in an upcoming version."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001782 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001783 "=head1 CAVEATS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001784 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001785 "=head2 SPECIAL CARE WITH SPECIAL COMPARISONS IN SETS AND BAGS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001786 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001787 "If you use certain special comparisons within a bag or set comparison there is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001788 "a danger that a test will fail when it should have passed. It can only happen"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001789 "if two or more special comparisons in the bag are competing to match elements."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001790 "Consider this comparison"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001791 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001792 "  cmp_deeply(['furry', 'furball'], bag(re(\"^fur\"), re(\"furb\")))"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001793 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001794 "There are two things that could happen, hopefully C<re(\"^fur\")> is paired with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001795 "\"furry\" and C<re(\"^furb\")> is paired with \"furb\" and everything is fine but it"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001796 "could happen that C<re(\"^fur\")> is paired with \"furball\" and then C<re(\"^furb\")>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001797 "cannot find a match and so the test fails. Examples of other competing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001798 "comparisons are C<bag(1, 2, 2)> vs C<set(1, 2)> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001799 "C<< methods(m1 => \"v1\", m2 => \"v2\") >> vs C<< methods(m1 => \"v1\") >>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001800 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001801 "This problem is could be solved by using a slower and more complicated"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001802 "algorithm for set and bag matching. Something for the future..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001803 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001804 "=head1 WHAT ARE SPECIAL COMPARISONS?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001805 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001806 "A special comparison (SC) is simply an object that inherits from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001807 "Test::Deep::Cmp. Whenever C<$expected_v> is an SC then instead of checking"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001808 "C<$got_v eq $expected_v>, we pass control over to the SC and let it do its"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001809 "thing."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001810 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001811 "Test::Deep exports lots of SC constructors, to make it easy for you to use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001812 "them in your test scripts. For example is C<re(\"hello\")> is just a handy way"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001813 "of creating a Test::Deep::Regexp object that will match any string containing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001814 "\"hello\". So"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001815 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001816 "  cmp_deeply([ 'a', 'b', 'hello world'], ['a', 'b', re(\"^hello\")]);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001817 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001818 "will check C<'a' eq 'a'>, C<'b' eq 'b'> but when it comes to comparing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001819 "C<'hello world'> and C<re(\"^hello\")> it will see that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001820 "$expected_v is an SC and so will pass control to the Test::Deep::Regexp class"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001821 "by do something like C<< $expected_v->descend($got_v) >>. The C<descend()>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001822 "method should just return true or false."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001823 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001824 "This gives you enough to write your own SCs but I haven't documented how"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001825 "diagnostics works because it's about to get an overhaul (theoretically)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001826 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001827 "=head1 EXPORTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001828 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001829 "By default, Test::Deep will export everything in its C<v0> tag, as if you had"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001830 "written:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001831 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001832 "  use Test::Deep ':v0';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001833 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001834 "Those things are:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001835 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001836 "  all any array array_each arrayelementsonly arraylength arraylengthonly bag"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001837 "  blessed bool cmp_bag cmp_deeply cmp_methods cmp_set code eq_deeply hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001838 "  hash_each hashkeys hashkeysonly ignore Isa isa listmethods methods noclass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001839 "  none noneof num obj_isa re reftype regexpmatches regexponly regexpref"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001840 "  regexprefonly scalarrefonly scalref set shallow str subbagof subhashof"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001841 "  subsetof superbagof superhashof supersetof useclass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001842 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001843 "A slightly better set of exports is the C<v1> set.  It's all the same things,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001844 "with the exception of C<Isa> and C<blessed>.  If you want to import"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001845 "\"everything\", you probably want to C<< use Test::Deep ':V1'; >>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001846 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001847 "There's another magic export group:  C<:preload>.  If that is specified, all of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001848 "the Test::Deep plugins will be loaded immediately instead of lazily."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001849 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001850 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001851 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001852 "L<Test::More>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001853 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001854 "=head1 THANKS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001855 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001856 "Thanks to Michael G Schwern for Test::More's is_deeply function which inspired"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001857 "this library."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001858 ""
